Description: edge-fan Markdown notes over an ordinary folder
 Fan Fold is a Qt 6 desktop note shell that edits ordinary Markdown files in a
 folder the user chooses. Notes are never copied into an application database,
 so the folder stays readable, greppable and syncable by any other tool.
 .
 The window rests at the screen edge and fans the notes out as overlapping
 cards. It provides a recursive library with search, bounded offline rich-text
 editors, autosave with conflict recovery, archive and restore, desktop trash,
 movable pinned note windows, per-note paper and ink colours, and global
 typography and layout settings.
 .
 The editor runtime is vendored offline; Fan Fold loads no content from a CDN
 or any other network source.
